NAME
       c2c-mcp - the model context protocol server of the cache-to-cache
       house

SYNOPSIS
       c2c-mcp [-e ENGINE] [--transport stdio|http] [--host HOST]
               [--port PORT] [--api-key KEY] [--verbose]

DESCRIPTION
       The server speaks JSON-RPC 2.0 — on stdio (the default, one line
       per message), or over HTTP (POST /, one request, one answer). It
       publishes the tools of the trade; the client calls the tools; the
       server does not call the clients — the wire between models does
       not ring the harness into loops.

       The three tools, as the interface ships them:

       c2c_register_pair
              receiver, sharer (required); engine, weights_path (optional).
              Declare a collaboration; returns the canonical pair id.
              The weights_path, when given, must name a .pt inside the zoo
              root (C2C_ZOO_ROOT): an agent's weights come from the zoo.

       c2c_fuse
              model, prompt (required). Fuse the pair's caches over the
              prompt; the report returns the gates and the ranks — the
              instrument panel of the collaboration, no answer generated.

       c2c_ask
              model, prompt (required); max_tokens, temperature (optional).
              Ask the pair through the full pipeline: resolve, capture,
              fuse, generate. Returns the answer text.

       The protocol version advertised: 2025-06-18. Notifications are
       acknowledged in silence, as the specification requires; unknown
       methods answer with the standard JSON-RPC error objects.

OPTIONS
       -e, --engine ENGINE    engine adapter for auto-built models
       --transport stdio      the default: stdin in, stdout out
       --transport http       JSON-RPC over HTTP, on --host:--port
       --host HOST            http only; default 127.0.0.1, and wisely so
       --port PORT            http only; default 8789
       --api-key KEY          http only; require Authorization: Bearer KEY.
                              A bind off the loopback will not start without
                              one; the loopback itself may stand open, as the
                              pipe is the trust. (C2C_API_KEY serves alike.)
       --certfile FILE        http only; PEM certificate for TLS
       --keyfile FILE         http only; PEM key; together, TLS on the
                              wire, and the bearer token rides it sealed
       --verbose              report every request to stderr

EXIT STATUS
       0  the session, ended well
       1  the transport, misbound (a port already answered, or no such host)
       2  the usage, amiss — as a network bind without a key

EXAMPLES
       The client, the standard input, the standard output::

           {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "tools/call",
            "params": {"name": "c2c_fuse", "arguments": {
              "model": "c2c/math-small+coder-small",
              "prompt": "what is two plus two?"}}}

